---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---
<Layout title="About Find Local" description="Why Find Local exists, how it collects events straight from venue calendars across 47 US cities, and how to get in touch." canonicalPath="/about">
  <article class="prose">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about' }]} />
    <h1>About Find Local</h1>
    <p>
      The idea for Find Local is credited to co-founder Alden Harris-McCoy, who, like me, thinks social media no longer serves
      its original intent of keeping us connected and informed. We rely on those platforms to know what's going on around us
      that's worth knowing, and to advertise our own events and gatherings — and they've become a poor way to do it. Every
      person who has worked on this project agrees: local artists, venues, gatherings, community and friends form the backbone
      of the cities we live in and the lives we want to lead. It's time there was a place that helped you find the treasures in
      your backyard without the noise. It's time to find local.
    </p>
    <p class="faint"><em>Elliot Harris, Co-Founder</em></p>

    <h2>So what is Find Local?</h2>
    <p>
      Find Local is a free site for finding the best local events. See what's happening in music, theater, comedy and more
      across <a href="/">47 US cities</a>, in an ever-expanding catalog that's updated daily. Filter by date, category, price
      and time of day, browse the <a href="/?view=map">map</a>, or follow a <a href="/venues">venue</a> you love.
      No account needed — saved events live in your own browser.
    </p>

    <h2>How?</h2>
    <p>
      Our pipeline reads the public calendars of thousands of local venues — music halls, comedy clubs, theaters, bars,
      community spaces — and turns them into one structured, searchable feed. Every listing links back to the venue or its
      own ticketing page so you can check the details at the source. If a venue isn't here yet but its calendar is online,
      email <a href="mailto:findlocalinternal@gmail.com">findlocalinternal@gmail.com</a> and it will be added promptly.
    </p>

    <h2>The team</h2>
    <p>
      Find Local is a team of friends, family and volunteers with a broad range of skills — marketing, software, business
      strategy, venue relations and promotion. Each member plays an essential role in making this a reality.
    </p>

    <h2>FAQs</h2>
    <h3>How does Find Local make money?</h3>
    <p>
      We mostly don't. We're volunteers with a passion for promoting local artists and businesses, and we believe some things
      are worth doing even if you don't get paid. Some outbound links may be affiliate links; that never changes the price
      you pay or which events we show.
    </p>
    <h3>Would you be open to making money?</h3>
    <p>
      Of course — it would let us broaden the scope and speed at which we operate. For business inquiries (affiliate links,
      advertising, partnering, data licensing) email <a href="mailto:findlocalinternal@gmail.com">findlocalinternal@gmail.com</a>
      or see the <a href="/platform">developer platform</a> and <a href="/developers">developer docs</a>.
    </p>
    <h3>I want to help. How?</h3>
    <p>
      Tell us about missing venues, broken listings or a city you'd like covered. If you're interested in helping in a more
      committed way, email us a brief synopsis of your skills and interest.
    </p>
    <h3>Why not just ask ChatGPT what's happening?</h3>
    <p>
      AI assistants are heavily biased toward what's already popular, so you're unlikely to discover new places; Find Local
      lists every event equally. They're prone to hallucinations; Find Local always links you back to the real source so you
      can check for yourself. (And if you do like asking an assistant, our <a href="/platform">MCP server</a> gives it
      real, sourced data.)
    </p>
    <h3>I want to report a bug, request a feature, or request a city or event.</h3>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:findlocalinternal@gmail.com">findlocalinternal@gmail.com</a> with the details — thank you for
      your engagement!
    </p>
    <h3>How can I stay updated?</h3>
    <p><a href="https://www.instagram.com/findl0cal/" rel="noopener">Follow us on Instagram</a> and read the <a href="/blog">blog</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
